  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org looks like this:\r\n![html-header](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/498917/30103275-651301e0-92f2-11e7-93e1-4f28c4ebcd6c.png)\r\n\r\nAnd https://dom.spec.whatwg.org looks like this:\r\n![dom-header](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/498917/30103290-737ec5ca-92f2-11e7-8851-b1bbd0ce9dcd.png)\r\n\r\nI think HTML would be clearer if organized like our other standards. The bits that don't have obvious place:\r\n* Multipage Version, One-Page Version, Developer Version and PDF Version. Suggest an \"Other versions\" heading for those, with multipage highlighted with a bouncing red arrow or something.\r\n* FAQ, suggest a separate heading.\r\n\r\nSee also https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2906",
